{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/965389-help-with-legacy-scales-of-balance","id":965389,"title":"Help with Legacy, Scales of Balance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-07T18:17:31-07:00","id":965389,"title":"Help with Legacy, Scales of Balance","content":"Some backstory and notes of how I want to use it<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hierarch Apollo\u2019s Scheme</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cThe final years of the \u201cColonel Movement\u201d found Athens of 1974 rebuilding itself towards democracy; The Seer\u2019s influence was weakening. Sentinel Apollo was a prominent Adamantine Arrow during the Athenian Pentacle Rebellion that followed. With most of the Council dead, he assumed the mantle of the Hierarch and drive the conflict into truce. The Silver Ladder honored him by sharing some secrets with the Arrow. Many years later, still obsessed with balancing the supernatural powers in Athens but seeing himself as the only capable individual, he has a scheme in place to remain in Power and restore the supernatural Scales of Balance.</i></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Control Council Votes;</i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> He is the Hierarch; 2/6 votes, Old Friend &amp; Cabal Mate with Councilor Dracon (Ladder); 1/6 votes, Cabal Mate with Councilor Noimon (Guardian); 1/6 votes. Total \u2154 of Consilium Votes</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Lex Magica Control;</i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Since he controls most votes he can pass/alter laws on Lex Magica. Lex Magica amplifies his power, protects his interest. As long it is considered Consilium Business he can use Lex Magica a) as Yantra on spells (+5dice), b) to protect from social or magical influence (rolls take -5dice).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Tolerate the Unnaturals;</i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The first thing he did as a hierarch was seeking alliances with other supernaturals (Werewolfs, Demons, etc). As long as they would not interfere with mage politics or young mortals, they could prey with discretion on elderly or criminal humans without fear of the Mage Council. The truce does not prevent however mage with relatives to retaliate.</span></span><br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernal Cold War;</span></span></b></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> After winning some decisive battles against the Seers, he forced them to propose a truce. Since then, no Seer is allowed within 500m of Revealed Pentacle Sancta and vice versa. Casting on/to foreign territory is punishable by death.</span></span><br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scales of Balance;</span></span></b></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The key in manipulating the Supernatural Politics is the Hierarch\u2019s legacy, the \u201cScales of Balance\u201d.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> tl;dr: Hierarch uses Prime, Lex Magica and Supernatural Politics to control the Consilium<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scales of Balance</span></span></b><br /> <br /> While the concepts of \u201cMetron Ariston\u201d \u201cYing and Yang\u201d are known since antiquity, the first formal mentions of the legacy are in Ladder documents during Nero\u2019s rule. While the core beliefs of the legacy is about balance, there are always rogue groups that try to use it as a way to gain power, harnessing the control over the supernatural forces of the cosmos as weapons.<br /> <br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Acanthus, Silver Ladder or Adamantine Arrow<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Prime 2, Politics 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Work out difference between supernatural entities<br /> <b>Organisation:</b> The legacy splits between three factions. The Scales of Enlightment (Silver Ladder faction) that hold the supernal into equilibrium so that mortals can awaken properly, The Veils of Balance (Adamantine Arrow faction) that use it as weapons against supernatural conflicts and the Scales of Balance proper that are no organisation.<br /> <b>Theory:</b> The legacy is based around the concept of \u201cMystica Res\u201d. Latin for \u201cMystical Things\u201d, it\u2019s a reference to the net sum of occult phenomena (spells, ghosts, vampires, etc) in a region, echoing a universe where anything is possible; a Supernal World. When the flux of Mystica Res is low, the Fallen World is derived of miracles, coming closer to the Lie. When the flux of Mystica Res is high, the natural laws become dangerously abstract for mortals to inhabit with Werewolfs waging war on Vampires. The answer lies somewhere in between; finding the Golden Ratio in the supernatural Scales of Balance for the mortal soul to ascend.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> <b>Cosmic Balance</b> (Sacred Geometry, Unveiling Prime Duration, Adv Duration +1R)<br /> <b>Requirements:</b> Initiation<br /> <i>To perceive upcoming supernatural alterations, a Scale must attune to the Cosmic Balance.</i><br /> By meditating for a scene, a Scale able to perceive ley lines and Nodes.<br /> Optional <b>Fate 1</b>:<br /> <i>One can sense the ripples of Mystica Res estimating the supernatural weight ley lines/nodes have on the world.</i><br /> In game terms storyteller informs (or guides) the player of a place that something significantly supernatural will happen, potentially disrupting the local supernatural ecosystem.<br /> <br /> <b>Cast with the Flow</b> (Supernal Veil, Veiling Prime Duration, reflexive +1R, no Optional)<br /> Requirements: Prime 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <i>To influence the supernatural, one requires casting spells without disturbing the Mystica Res. While not a permanently hidden, it is enough to catch victims off-guard and if passed unnoticed maybe none will investigate at all.</i><br /> By spending one point of mana as an instant action the caster can make his spells \u201cinvisible\u201d. Passive abilities (Peripheral Mage Sight) fail to detect them while activated ones trigger Clash of Wills.<br /> Optional <b>Fate 2</b>: As above but the attainment can be activated as reflexive action or incorporated into an Imago, making the spell \u201cinvisible\u201d, even during casting it. Other mages trigger a Clash of Wills to detect both the casting and the spell itself as a Supernal phenomenon.<br /> <br /> <b>Occult Whispers</b> (Words of Truth, Ruling Prime of Potency 4, Composure, Influence/Guilty +1R, Adv Duration +1R, Sensory +1R)<br /> Requirements: Prime 3, Politics 3<br /> <i>By studying the pattern of an entity for one scene, a Scale can shape the current of Mystica Res to influence the entity, tuning it to its inner supernatural calling.</i><br /> The Scale makes a social maneuvering roll, as the mage focuses on an entity for a scene talking to its supernal conscience. If the entity follows the call, it gains the Inspired Condition for one day, else it gains the Guilty Condition.<br /> Optional <b>Fate 3</b> (Shifting the Odds):<br /> <i>The Scale can not only influence the entity but also it\u2019s short term destiny, nudging conditions into a desired supernatural situation.</i><br /> The attainment also fabricates fortune of the target into what the Scale has in mind as per Shifting the Odds spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Complanate in Statera</b> (Geomancy, Weaving Prime of Duration, Lasting +2R)<br /> Requirements: Prime 4, Politics 4<br /> <i>For the world to achieve cosmic balance one should alter it one step at a time. Altering Mystica Res requires the tuning the right resonance in the right place.</i><br /> Attuning near a ley line or Node for a scene allows the mage by spending 1 mana to permanently alter its resonance into something that will influence the supernatural ecosystem accordingly. (Ex. From &quot;Sorrow&quot; to &quot;Peace&quot; resonance)<br /> Optional <b>Fate 4</b> (Strings of Fate):<br /> <i>The resonance becomes so attuned with the Mystica Res that it forces entities towards its resonance.</i><br /> As long as an entity falls under the influence of that node/ley line (by long time exposure, proximity, etc), it's actions will nudge actions to work towards what the mage specified (related with the supernatural) at least once per day. (Ex. Werewolfs near the &quot;Peace&quot; Node will be presented with non-aggresive options to solve problems with neiboring Spirits and Vampires, as the mage specified it)<br /> <br /> <b>Mystica Res</b> (Aetheric Winds+Ephemeral Enchantment, Faying Prime of Potency, Assign Potency to destroy mana +1R, Instant +1R, Sensory +1R)<br /> Requirements: Prime 5, Politics 5<br /> <i>Sometimes negotiating is not an option, but those that level the scale are not afraid. By tapping the supernatural potential difference of the area, they can harm any kind of creature (whether in twilight or not) with the raw occult power.</i><br /> By spending one point of mana as an instant action, the Scale can inflict up to 7 points of lethal damage within his sensory range. Alternatively, she may reduce the damage by an amount to destroy an equal amount of supernatural power source (mana, essence, etc).<br /> Optional <b>Fate 5</b> (Forge Destiny):<br /> <i>Shaping the target\u2019s source of occult power, the Scale can alter the subject\u2019s interaction with Mystical Res, shaping his encounter with the supernatural.</i><br /> As per Forge Destiny spell, but the effects must be closely related with the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","user":"Shadowjim12","date":". 02-14-2017, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:26:36-07:00","id":965449,"title":"","content":"Second attainment seems to be how Veiling spells work anyway, not sure on your definition of Passive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:22:27-07:00","id":965535,"title":"","content":"How Veiling works, yes, but the Attainment lets you use any spell that way, without attracting attention. It's a neat ability. as for the Passive thing... I guess they meant that one must be actively looking for an effect even to have a chance at detecting it, by winning a Clash of Wills. You just can't find them by chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:06:08-07:00","id":965726,"title":"","content":"I noticed that I lack some optional effects.<br /> Are they mandatory? What would you twick to evocate the theme of supernatural manipulator/negotiator better?<br /> <br /> Also, are the attainments within resonable scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:53:00-07:00","id":965883,"title":"","content":"Optional effects are not mandatory, but is usually better to have them than not, unless that would dilute or mess up the concept and feel tacked on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:34:07-07:00","id":965969,"title":"","content":"From the attainments I gather that The Scales at the higher end of the legacy aren't there merely to observe. Indeed, they abuse the observer effect and how it can alter supernatural occurrences Maybe abuse is too strong a term, they influence those effects. Either way, the ability to manipulate Fate might be pertinent, by endowing Blessings of Hexes. I do encourage you to come up with things that aren't necessarily dice related. I feel like narrative influences might be the key to realizing this legacy's potential with Optional Attainments relating to Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T14:24:29-08:00","id":1048931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/965389-help-with-legacy-scales-of-balance?p=965969#post965969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the attainments I gather that The Scales at the higher end of the legacy aren't there merely to observe... Maybe abuse is too strong a term, they influence those effects... I feel like narrative influences might be the key to realizing this legacy's potential with Optional Attainments relating to Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mrmdubois, you got the theme precisely.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, the rest seem to be more in line. Though, I seem to brainfart about the final Attainment for like 5 months now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T14:32:01-08:00","id":1048938,"title":"","content":"The damage effect on that fifth attainment should only be 5 Lethal. Reach expenditure for the Optional Fate effect should be noted, I presume it's activated as a ritual with Reach spent on Advanced Duration so it will last a year, correct?<br /> <br /> The Inspired or Guilty Condition from Occult Whispers should probably last until it's expended or the Duration runs out. Depending on the circumstances it could and should last more than a day. Also this is essentially the Scales one-way walky-talky since the target will be able to hear the Scale speak to him for the entire Duration unless the Scale ends the effect early. You have 2 Reach to spend for the Shifting the Odds part of that attainment.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about the Fate Optional for the second attainment, maybe it's just me but it seems sort of lackluster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-14-2017, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T23:39:13-08:00","id":1049719,"title":"","content":"I really like the second attainment. Elegant, simple and useful. Very good work.<br /> <br /> I'm however not sure I like the last one. It seems a bit too rough for these guys. How about something to the effect of removing all their mana and giving them a condition to impede casting?<br /> That would be worthy of an iron fisted ruler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12700-hellocthulhu","name":"HelloCthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}